For every $h\in A_T$, every $\ell,\beta\in\widetilde T$, and every integer $r$, $$\label{eq:two-point-duality}
 K^r_{\ell\beta}(h)
   =K^{-2-r}_{\beta\ell}(h^{-1}).$$ If $J,J'\subseteq T$, the rows with indices outside $\widetilde J'$ are unchanged by left multiplication of $h$ by $A_{J'}$, and the columns with indices outside $\widetilde J$ are unchanged by right multiplication of $h$ by $A_J$.

Let $R$ be a minimal complex with a single simple $U_\ell$ at $(0,0)$ and shifted right projectives, and let $r\ge-1$ bound its normalized levels. Applying a right inverse twist, and then minimizing, does not increase this bound. The same holds for the product of inverse twists in one color. At the acted vertex $\alpha$, the test complexes satisfy $$\label{eq:two-point-inverse-test}
 (R D_\alpha)e_\alpha
       \simeq (Re_\alpha)\langle-2\rangle[-1].$$
